@startuml state-fp-ephemeralstream
!define STREAM_COLOR #E8F5E9
!define RAF_COLOR #FFF3E0
!define LISTENER_COLOR #E3F2FD

title EphemeralStream: Demand-Driven RAF Batching

participant "mousemove Event\nHandler" as events
participant "EphemeralStream" as stream
participant "RAF Scheduler" as raf
participant "React Signal\n(Subscriber A)" as subA
participant "Canvas Render\n(Subscriber B)" as subB

note over events, subB
  **Scenario:** User moves mouse rapidly (60+ events/second)
  Expected: Highest frequency without jank
end note

== Fast Event Burst (10ms) ==
events -> stream: emit({x: 100, y: 50})
activate stream
note right of stream
  **emit() logic:**
  1. Update _last value
  2. Mark AnimatedEntry.pending
  3. Schedule ONE RAF (if not already pending)
  4. DON'T call listeners yet
end note

stream -> stream: _last = {x: 100, y: 50}
stream -> stream: AnimatedEntry.pending = _last
stream -> stream: if (!rafPending) requestAnimationFrame(flush)
stream -> raf: requestAnimationFrame(flushAnimated)
note right of raf
  RAF scheduled once
  Not per #emit() call
end note
deactivate stream

events -> stream: emit({x: 105, y: 48})
activate stream
stream -> stream: _last = {x: 105, y: 48}
stream -> stream: AnimatedEntry.pending = _last
note right of stream
  rafPending = true (already scheduled)
  DON'T call requestAnimationFrame again
  Just update the pending value
end note
deactivate stream

events -> stream: emit({x: 110, y: 45})
activate stream
stream -> stream: _last = {x: 110, y: 45}
stream -> stream: AnimatedEntry.pending = _last
deactivate stream

... (dozens more events) ...

== Browser Frame Callback (16ms) ==
raf -> stream: flushAnimated callback fires
activate stream
note right of stream
  **flushAnimated() logic:**
  For each AnimatedEntry where hasPending:
    1. get last buffered value
    2. call listener with THAT value
  Then reset hasPending flags
end note

stream -> subA: subA_listener({x: 110, y: 45})
note right of subA
  React signal updated
  Once per frame maximum
  No jank, smooth 60fps
end note

stream -> subB: subB_listener({x: 110, y: 45})
note right of subB
  Canvas draw call
  No redundant redraws
  Efficient batching
end note

deactivate stream

== Unsubscribe & Cleanup ==
subA -> stream: unsubscribe()
activate stream
stream -> stream: animatedListeners.delete(subA)
note right of stream
  If no more animated listeners:
    cancelAnimationFrame(rafId)
  Stream now idle = 0 CPU cost
end note
deactivate stream

note over events, subB
  **Benefits:**
  ✓ Single RAF per stream (not per-subscriber)
  ✓ Latest value delivered (last-value semantics)
  ✓ Zero CPU when stream idle (no coalescing overhead)
  ✓ Safe for high-frequency (mouse, scroll, drag, canvas)
  ✓ Synchronous subscribe() for instant access to last value
end note

@enduml
